\tempo sets the tempo for a bar.
It must be included inside a bar definition,
otherwise it will throw an error.
Its syntax is the following:

\tempo 120

or

\tempo 4 = 80

The line above defines the duration for a
quarter note, while the first line
defines the tempo for the duration set
with the \time command.

When a tempo is set, it is held for all
bars defined after it, until a new tempo is set.
For this reason, when setting a new tempo,
it should be set at the beginning of the bar,
like the example below.

\bar tempo-1 {
    \tempo 4 = 120
    \inst c'4 cis'8 c' b4
}
